  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Andy Chakalis A native Clevelander, Andrew Chakalis attended Brush High School and Case Western Reserve University, where his Italian language studies earned him the Italian Fellowship to the Academy of Fine Arts in Florence in 1966. The school term breaks provided him the opportunity to assist at the marble quarries in Carrara, work at ceramic kilns in Faenza, and later work with internationally renowned sculptor Arnoldo Pomodoro in Milan. Upon returning to Cleveland in 1970, Chakalis worked in product development and design before joining The..."
    ]
  },
